Each hypothesis is one scope line the seller agreed to deliver, as written in the scope document; value is null.

{
  "documents": [
    {
      "title": "Agreed website scope",
      "text": "Website build quote, accepted by buyer\nSeller: Kavya, independent web designer in India\nBuyer: Neel, owner of fictional shop Mithi Nest\nProject price: USD 480\n\nAgreed requirements:\nBuild a five-page website: Home, About, Products, FAQ and Contact.\nAdd a WhatsApp inquiry button on every page.\nProvide a mobile performance report for the finished website.\nEnter all 20 buyer-supplied product descriptions on the Products page.\n\nBuyer will supply the text and product descriptions. Seller will hand over the finished site files and a short note. Any work outside these four requirements needs a separate agreement. Neel accepted this scope and the price before work began; payment is for the service, not for physical goods."
    },
    {
      "title": "Website handover note",
      "text": "Handover from Kavya to Neel\n\nHi Neel, website files ready hain. The handover folder contains the site files, product images and setup notes. The navigation includes Home, About, Products, FAQ and Contact; all five pages are included in the handover.\n\nThe Products page has 12 of the 20 supplied descriptions. The other eight are still to be entered. There is no WhatsApp inquiry button in the delivered files; I did not add one.\n\nI have attached the mobile performance report to the handover email. Please review the folder and let me know if anything needs attention. The folder also includes a short guide for updating the page text."
    },
    {
      "title": "Post-delivery chat",
      "text": "Neel, 10:05: Files mil gaye, thanks. I opened the site and can see all five pages in the menu.\n\nKavya, 10:09: Great. Setup notes bhi folder mein hain, so you can update the text later.\n\nNeel, 10:14: Products page par sirf 12 descriptions dikh rahe hain. I had sent 20.\n\nKavya, 10:18: Haan, eight entries remain. I will arrange a time to finish them.\n\nNeel, 10:22: Also, I cannot see the WhatsApp inquiry button on any page.\n\nKavya, 10:25: Correct, I did not include it in this delivery. Let's discuss when I can add it.\n\nNeel, 10:30: The handover email mentions a performance report; I will check it separately."
    }
  ],
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "text": "Build a five-page website: Home, About, Products, FAQ and Contact.",
      "value": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Add a WhatsApp inquiry button on every page.",
      "value": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Provide a mobile performance report for the finished website.",
      "value": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Enter all 20 buyer-supplied product descriptions on the Products page.",
      "value": null
    }
  ]
}
